-- title:
--   Theorem 20 — $\mathbb P_{x\sim[-1,1]^m}[Z_{\mathbf 1+x}\subseteq Z]\ge e^{-2n}$
-- statement:
--   Let $A\in\mathbb R^{m\times n}$ be any real matrix with rows $a_1,\dots,a_m$ and let $Z=Z_{\mathbf1}$ be the zonotope they generate. For $x$ drawn uniformly from the solid cube $[-1,1]^m$, rescale the $i$-th generator by $1+x_i\in[0,2]$. Then
--   $$\mathbb P_{x\sim[-1,1]^m}\big[Z_{\mathbf 1+x}\subseteq Z\big]\ge e^{-2n}.$$
--   No rank assumption is made; $A=0$ and rank-deficient matrices are included.
--
--   A random rescaling of the segments thus stays inside the original zonotope with probability at least exponential in the dimension $n$, independently of the number $m$ of segments. Corollary 21 deduces the coordinate-section bounds used in §5.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: P_{x∼[−1,1]^m}[Z_{1+x} ⊆ Z] → Vol_m({x : Z_{1+x} ⊆ Z} ∩ [−1,1]^m)/2^m; reason: on the cube the event is an intersection of closed halfspaces, hence measurable
-- source:
--   Victor Reis, Thomas Rothvoss, Linear-size ℓ1 sparsifiers, STOC 2027 submission #162 (October 2026; PDF SHA-256 5137e7dee3cd303bd508f90f5f42c955632af5dc2ec978d9ef575bae4ce23710), §4.1, Theorem 20, p.11

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_L1Sparsifiers_Main_Zonotope
import Definitions.Def_L1Sparsifiers_Main_UniformCube

namespace L1Sparsifiers.Main

/-- **Theorem 20** (p.11). "Let Z ⊆ ℝⁿ be a zonotope generated by the rows of A ∈ ℝ^{m×n}. Then
P_{x∼[−1,1]^m}[Z_{1+x} ⊆ Z] ≥ e^{−2n}."

Every real matrix is allowed (any rank, including `A = 0`). -/
theorem theorem_20 {m n : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) ℝ) :
    Real.exp (-2 * (n : ℝ)) ≤ cubeProb m {x | zonotope A (1 + x) ⊆ zonotope A 1} := by sorry

end L1Sparsifiers.Main
